<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<introduction xml:id="intro" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <p>
        Math 97 - Intermediate Algebra is the study of algebra involving 
        exponents. It is also preparation for the study of functions in 
        precalculus and calculus. 
    </p>
    <p>
        During the quarter we will focus on:
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Factoring of quadratic expressions
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Solving quadratic equations
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Simplifying rational expressions
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Simplifying radical expressions
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
        These notes will include examples, which include video examples, if
        you are viewing them online as well as practice exercises for the notetaker.
        Homework for this material can be found on our WAMAP course page.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you have any questions or notice any mistakes in these notes,
        please reach out to me via email or visit me in my office in Cedar
        Hall 301 during my student help hours.
    </p>
    <p>
        Math fans, let's get started!
    </p>
</introduction>
